Resolving ClassNotFoundException in Java

The ClassNotFoundException in Java occurs when the Java Virtual Machine (JVM) cannot find the class specified in the code. 
This exception typically arises when the classloader fails to load a class at runtime.

Example

try {
Class.forName("com.example.NonExistentClass");
} catch (ClassNotFoundException e) {
e.printStackTrace();
}
